msgid "Code style and language versions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:18
msgid ""
"Consistent code style and language version choices make ROS packages easier "
"to read, review, maintain, and integrate. This article describes the coding "
"standards, naming conventions, formatting expectations, and recommended "
"tooling for C, C++, Python, and related ROS development workflows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:27
msgid "Table of Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:29
msgid ""
"In order to achieve a consistent looking product we will all follow "
"externally (if possible) defined style guidelines for each language. For "
"other things like package layout or documentation layout we will need to "
"come up with our own guidelines, drawing on current, popular styles in use "
"now."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:32
msgid ""
"Additionally, wherever possible, developers should use integrated tools to "
"allow them to check that these guidelines are followed in their editors. For "
"example, everyone should have a PEP8 checker built into their editor to cut "
"down on review iterations related to style."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:35
msgid ""
"Also where possible, packages should check style as part of their unit tests "
"to help with the automated detection of style issues (see `ament_lint_auto "
"<https://github.com/ament/ament_lint/blob/rolling/ament_lint_auto/doc/index."
"rst>`__)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:38
msgid "C"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:41
#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:76
msgid "Standard"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:43
msgid "We will target C17."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:46
#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:81
#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:355
#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:400
msgid "Style"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:48
msgid ""
"We will use `Python's PEP7 <https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0007/>`__ "
"for our C style guide, with some modifications and additions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:50
msgid ""
"We will target C17, as we do not need to support C89 (as PEP7 recommends)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:52
msgid ""
"rationale: among other things it allows us to use both ``//`` and ``/* */`` "
"style comments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:53
msgid "rationale: C17 is pretty much ubiquitous now"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:55
msgid "C++ style ``//`` comments are allowed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:56
msgid ""
"(optional) Always place literals on the left-hand side of comparison "
"operators, e.g. ``0 == ret`` instead of ``ret == 0``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:58
msgid "rationale: ``ret == 0`` too easily turns into ``ret = 0`` by accident"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:59
msgid ""
"optional because when using ``-Wall`` (or equivalent) modern compilers will "
"warn you when this happens"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:61
msgid ""
"All of the following modifications only apply if we are not writing Python "
"modules:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:63
msgid "Do not use ``Py_`` as a prefix for everything"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:65
msgid ""
"instead use a CamelCase version of the package name or other appropriate "
"prefix"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:67
msgid "The stuff about documentation strings doesn't apply"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:69
msgid ""
"We can use the `pep7 <https://github.com/mike-perdide/pep7>`__ python module "
"for style checking. The editor integration seems slim, we may need to look "
"into automated checking for C in more detail."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:73
msgid "C++"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:78
msgid "Rolling targets C++20."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:84
msgid ""
"We will use the `Google C++ Style Guide <https://google.github.io/styleguide/"
"cppguide.html>`__, with some modifications:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:87
msgid "Line Length"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:89
msgid "Our maximum line length is 100 characters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:92
msgid "File Extensions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:94
msgid "Header files should use the ``.hpp`` extension."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:96
#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:100
msgid "rationale: Allow tools to determine content of files, C++ or C."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:98
msgid "Implementation files should use the ``.cpp`` extension."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:103
msgid "Variable Naming"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:105
msgid ""
"For global variables use lowercase with underscores prefixed with ``g_``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:107
msgid "rationale: keep variable naming case consistent across the project"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:108
msgid "rationale: easy to tell the scope of a variable at a glance"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:109
msgid "consistency across languages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:111
msgid ""
"**Note on naming conventions**: ROS 2 deviates from the Google C++ Style "
"Guide in several naming areas:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:113
msgid ""
"The Google style guide recommends ``kPascalCase`` for constants (e.g., "
"``kDaysInAWeek``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:114
msgid ""
"ROS 2 projects currently use a mix of ``snake_case``, ``PascalCase``, and "
"``UPPER_CASE`` naming conventions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:115
msgid ""
"This deviation is for historical reasons and consistency with existing ROS "
"codebases"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:116
msgid ""
"For new projects, developers should follow the existing conventions in "
"related ROS 2 packages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:117
msgid ""
"When in doubt, prefer consistency with surrounding code over strict "
"adherence to Google style"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:120
msgid "Function and Method Naming"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:122
msgid ""
"Google style guide says ``CamelCase``, but the C++ std library's style of "
"``snake_case`` is also allowed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:124
msgid "rationale: ROS 2 core packages currently use ``snake_case``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:126
msgid ""
"reason: either an historical oversight or a personal preference that didn't "
"get checked by the linter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:127
msgid "reason for not changing: retroactively changing would be too disruptive"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:128
msgid "other considerations:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:130
msgid ""
"``cpplint.py`` does not check this case (hard to enforce other than with "
"review)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:131
msgid "``snake_case`` can result in more consistency across languages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:132
msgid "specific guidance:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:134
msgid "for existing projects, prefer the existing style"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:135
msgid ""
"for new projects, either is acceptable, but a preference for matching "
"related existing projects is advised"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:136
msgid "final decision is always developer discretion"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:138
msgid ""
"special cases like function pointers, callable types, etc. may require "
"bending the rules"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:139
msgid "Note that classes should still use ``CamelCase`` by default"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:142
msgid "Access Control"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:144
msgid ""
"Drop requirement for all class members to be private and therefore require "
"accessors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:146
msgid "rationale: this is overly constraining for user API design"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:147
msgid ""
"we should prefer private members, only making them public when they are "
"needed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:148
msgid ""
"we should consider using accessors before choosing to allow direct member "
"access"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:149
msgid ""
"we should have a good reason for allowing direct member access, other than "
"because it is convenient for us"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:152
msgid "Exceptions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:154
msgid "Exceptions are allowed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:156
msgid ""
"rationale: this is a new codebase, so the legacy argument doesn't apply to us"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:157
msgid ""
"rationale: for user-facing API's it is more idiomatic C++ to have exceptions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:158
msgid "Exceptions in destructors should be explicitly avoided"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:160
msgid ""
"We should consider avoiding Exceptions if we intend to wrap the resulting "
"API in C"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:162
msgid "rationale: it will make it easier to wrap in C"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:163
msgid ""
"rationale: most of our dependencies in code we intend to wrap in C do not "
"use exceptions anyways"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:166
msgid "Function-like Objects"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:168
msgid "No restrictions on Lambda's or ``std::function`` or ``std::bind``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:171
msgid "Boost"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:173
msgid "Boost should be avoided unless absolutely required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:176
msgid "Comments and Doc Comments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:178
msgid ""
"Use ``///`` and ``/** */`` comments for *documentation* purposes and ``//`` "
"style comments for notes and general comments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:180
msgid ""
"Class and Function comments should use ``///`` and ``/** */`` style comments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:181
msgid "rationale: these are recommended for Doxygen and Sphinx in C/C++"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:182
msgid ""
"rationale: mixing ``/* */`` and ``//`` is convenient for block commenting "
"out code which contains comments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:183
msgid ""
"Descriptions of how the code works or notes within classes and functions "
"should use ``//`` style comments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:186
msgid "Pointer Syntax Alignment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:188
msgid ""
"Use ``char * c;`` instead of ``char* c;`` or ``char *c;`` because of this "
"scenario ``char* c, *d, *e;``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:191
msgid "Class Privacy Keywords"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:193
msgid ""
"Do not put 1 space before ``public:``, ``private:``, or ``protected:``, it "
"is more consistent for all indentations to be a multiple of 2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:195
msgid ""
"rationale: most editors don't like indentations which are not a multiple of "
"the (soft) tab size"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:196
msgid ""
"Use zero spaces before ``public:``, ``private:``, or ``protected:``, or 2 "
"spaces"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:197
msgid ""
"If you use 2 spaces before, indent other class statements by 2 additional "
"spaces"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:198
msgid ""
"Prefer zero spaces, i.e. ``public:``, ``private:``, or ``protected:`` in the "
"same column as the class"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:201
msgid "Nested Templates"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:203
msgid "Never add whitespace to nested templates"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:205
msgid ""
"Prefer ``set<list<string>>`` (C++11 feature) to ``set<list<string> >`` or "
"``set< list<string> >``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:208
msgid "Always Use Braces"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:210
msgid ""
"Always use braces following ``if``, ``else``, ``do``, ``while``, and "
"``for``, even when the body is a single line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:212
msgid ""
"rationale: less opportunity for visual ambiguity and for complications due "
"to use of macros in the body"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:215
msgid "Open Versus Cuddled Braces"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:217
msgid ""
"Use open braces for ``function``, ``class``, ``enum``, and ``struct`` "
"definitions, but cuddle braces on ``if``, ``else``, ``while``, ``for``, "
"etc..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:219
msgid ""
"Exception: when an ``if`` (or ``while``, etc.) condition is long enough to "
"require line-wrapping, then use an open brace (i.e., don't cuddle)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:221
msgid ""
"When a function call cannot fit on one line, wrap at the open parenthesis "
"(not in between arguments) and start them on the next line with a 2-space "
"indent. Continue with the 2-space indent on subsequent lines for more "
"arguments. (Note that the `Google style guide <https://google.github.io/"
"styleguide/cppguide.html#Function_Calls>`__ is internally contradictory on "
"this point.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:225
msgid ""
"Same goes for ``if`` (and ``while``, etc.) conditions that are too long to "
"fit on one line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:228
msgid "Examples"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:230
#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:285
msgid "This is OK:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:232
msgid ""
"int main(int argc, char **argv)\n"
"{\n"
"  if (condition) {\n"
"    return 0;\n"
"  } else {\n"
"    return 1;\n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"if (this && that || both) {\n"
"  ...\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"// Long condition; open brace\n"
"if (\n"
"  this && that || both && this && that || both && this && that || both && "
"this && that)\n"
"{\n"
"  ...\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"// Short function call\n"
"call_func(foo, bar);\n"
"\n"
"// Long function call; wrap at the open parenthesis\n"
"call_func(\n"
"  foo, bar, foo, bar, foo, bar, foo, bar, foo, bar, foo, bar, foo, bar, foo, "
"bar, foo, bar,\n"
"  foo, bar, foo, bar, foo, bar, foo, bar, foo, bar, foo, bar, foo, bar, foo, "
"bar, foo, bar);\n"
"\n"
"// Very long function argument; separate it for readability\n"
"call_func(\n"
"  bang,\n"
"  fooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooo,\n"
"  bar, bat);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:268
msgid "This is **not** OK:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:270
msgid ""
"int main(int argc, char **argv) {\n"
"  return 0;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"if (this &&\n"
"    that ||\n"
"    both) {\n"
"  ...\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:283
msgid ""
"Use open braces rather than excessive indentation, e.g. for distinguishing "
"constructor code from constructor initializer lists"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:287
msgid ""
"ReturnType LongClassName::ReallyReallyReallyLongFunctionName(\n"
"  Type par_name1,  // 2 space indent\n"
"  Type par_name2,\n"
"  Type par_name3)\n"
"{\n"
"  DoSomething();  // 2 space indent\n"
"  ...\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"MyClass::MyClass(int var)\n"
": some_var_(var),\n"
"  some_other_var_(var + 1)\n"
"{\n"
"  ...\n"
"  DoSomething();\n"
"  ...\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:307
msgid "This is **not** OK, even weird (the google way?):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:309
msgid ""
"ReturnType LongClassName::ReallyReallyReallyLongFunctionName(\n"
"    Type par_name1,  // 4 space indent\n"
"    Type par_name2,\n"
"    Type par_name3) {\n"
"  DoSomething();  // 2 space indent\n"
"  ...\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"MyClass::MyClass(int var)\n"
"    : some_var_(var),             // 4 space indent\n"
"      some_other_var_(var + 1) {  // lined up\n"
"  ...\n"
"  DoSomething();\n"
"  ...\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:328
