#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:340
msgid ""
"We also run other tools to detect and eliminate as many warnings as "
"possible. Here's a non-exhaustive list of additional things we try to do on "
"all of our packages:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:343
msgid "use compiler flags like ``-Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:344
msgid ""
"run static code analysis like ``cppcheck``, which we have integrated in "
"`ament_cppcheck <https://github.com/ament/ament_lint/blob/rolling/"
"ament_cppcheck/doc/index.rst>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:347
msgid "Python"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:350
#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:394
msgid "Version"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:352
msgid "We will target Python 3 for our development."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:357
msgid ""
"We will use the `PEP8 guidelines <https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0008/"
">`_ for code format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:359
msgid ""
"We chose the following more precise rule where PEP 8 leaves some freedom:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:361
msgid ""
"`We allow up to 100 characters per line (fifth paragraph) <https://www."
"python.org/dev/peps/pep-0008/#maximum-line-length>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:362
msgid ""
"`We pick single quotes over double quotes as long as no escaping is "
"necessary <https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0008/#string-quotes>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:363
msgid ""
"`We prefer hanging indents for continuation lines <https://www.python.org/"
"dev/peps/pep-0008/#indentation>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:364
msgid ""
"`We prefer splitting having only one import per line <https://peps.python."
"org/pep-0008/#imports>`_:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:366
msgid ""
"# This is preferred\n"
"from typing import Dict\n"
"from typing import List\n"
"\n"
"# over these\n"
"from typing import Dict, List\n"
"from typing import (\n"
"  Dict,\n"
"  List,\n"
")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:379
msgid ""
"Tools like the ``(ament_)pycodestyle`` Python package should be used in unit-"
"test and/or editor integration for checking Python code style."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:381
msgid ""
"The pycodestyle configuration used in the linter is `here <https://github."
"com/ament/ament_lint/blob/rolling/ament_pycodestyle/ament_pycodestyle/"
"configuration/ament_pycodestyle.ini>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:383
msgid "Integration with editors:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:385
msgid "`atom <https://atom.io/packages/linter-pycodestyle>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:386
msgid "`emacs <https://www.emacswiki.org/emacs/PythonProgrammingInEmacs>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:387
msgid ""
"`Sublime Text <https://sublime.wbond.net/packages/SublimeLinter-flake8>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:388
msgid "`vim <https://github.com/nvie/vim-flake8>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:391
msgid "CMake"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:396
msgid ""
"Read `REP 2000 <https://reps.openrobotics.org/rep-2000/>`_ to determine the "
"minimum CMake version you should support. Currently the minimum version of "
"any supported ROS distro is **3.14.4** (ROS Humble on macOS)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:402
msgid ""
"Since there is not an existing CMake style guide we will define our own:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:404
msgid "Use lowercase command names (``find_package``, not ``FIND_PACKAGE``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:405
msgid "Use ``snake_case`` identifiers (variables, functions, macros)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:406
msgid "Use empty ``else()`` and ``end...()`` commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:407
msgid "No whitespace before ``(``\\ 's."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:408
msgid "Use two spaces of indentation, do not use tabs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:409
msgid ""
"Do not use aligned indentation for parameters of multi-line macro "
"invocations. Use two spaces only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:411
msgid "Prefer functions with ``set(PARENT_SCOPE)`` to macros."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:412
msgid ""
"When using macros prefix local variables with ``_`` or a reasonable prefix."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:415
msgid "Markdown / reStructured Text / docblocks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:417
msgid ""
"The following rules to format text is intended to increase readability as "
"well as versioning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:420
msgid "Any Doc Type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:422
msgid "Each sentence must start on a new line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:424
msgid ""
"Rationale: For longer paragraphs a single change in the beginning makes the "
"diff unreadable since it carries forward through the whole paragraph."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:426
msgid "Each sentence can optionally be wrapped to keep each line short."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:427
msgid "The lines should not have any trailing white spaces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:430
msgid "Markdown or RST"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:432
msgid ""
"Each section title should be preceded by one empty line and succeeded by one "
"empty line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:434
msgid ""
"Rationale: It expedites to get an overview about the structure when "
"screening the document."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:436
msgid "A code block must be preceded and succeeded by an empty line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:438
msgid ""
"Rationale: Whitespace is significant only directly before and directly after "
"fenced code blocks. Following these instructions will ensure that "
"highlighting works properly and consistently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:441
msgid "A code block should specify a syntax (e.g. ``bash``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:444
msgid "RST only"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:446
msgid ""
"In reStructured Text the headings should follow the hierarchy described in "
"the `Sphinx style guide <https://documentation-style-guide-sphinx."
"readthedocs.io/en/latest/style-guide.html#headings>`__:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:448
msgid "``#`` with overline (only once, used for the document title)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:449
msgid "``*`` with overline"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:450
msgid "``=``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:451
msgid "``-``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:452
msgid "``^``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:453
msgid "``\"``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:454
msgid ""
"Rationale: A consistent hierarchy expedites getting an idea about the "
"nesting level when screening the document."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:457
msgid "Markdown Only"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:459
msgid ""
"In Markdown the headings should follow the ATX-style described in the "
"`Markdown syntax documentation <https://daringfireball.net/projects/markdown/"
"syntax#header>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:461
msgid ""
"ATX-style headers use 1-6 hash characters (``#``) at the start of the line "
"to denote header levels 1-6."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:462
msgid ""
"A space between the hashes and the header title should be used (such as ``# "
"Heading 1``) to make it easier to visually separate them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:463
msgid ""
"Justification for the ATX-style preference comes from the `Google Markdown "
"style guide <https://github.com/google/styleguide/blob/gh-pages/docguide/"
"style.md#atx-style-headings>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Code-Style-Language-Versions.rst:464
msgid ""
"Rationale: ATX-style headers are easier to search and maintain, and make the "
"first two header levels consistent with the other levels."
msgstr ""
